From abd51dec138617c926b7efd0482366a29fd8957f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jocelyn Berrendonner <jocelynb@microsoft.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:18:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] mode: support HGX A100 8-GPU with six NVSwitches

An HGX A100 8-GPU baseboard carries six second-generation NVSwitch
chips (NVLink 3), while HGX H100 8-GPU carries four. Passing a full
A100 baseboard through to the VM exposes 8 GPUs and 6 NVSwitches,
which detection rejects with "unexpected topology: 6 NVSWITCH, 8 GPU,
0 PCI_SW_MNG".

Detect (6, 8, 0) as its own "nvl3" fabric. It starts nv-fabricmanager
with FABRIC_MODE=0 like NVL4, but without PARTITION_RAIL_POLICY: on
A100, fabric manager (seen with 580.159.04) rejects that key with

  unsupported config item PARTITION_RAIL_POLICY is specified in fabric
  manager config file

and exits with status 255 before it opens any NVSwitch. Without the
key, it configures all GPUs and NVSwitches.

NVL4 and NVL5 keep writing their rail policy as before.

Signed-off-by: Jocelyn Berrendonner <jocelynb@microsoft.com>
Assisted-by: GitHub Copilot
