From ba3fbd9223149159bfb79f780ac16cbc0050ff04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jocelyn Berrendonner <jocelynb@microsoft.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:37:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] daemon: fail the readiness wait when the daemon exits
 with an error

nvidia_persistenced() and nv_fabricmanager() spawn their daemon, then
wait for its readiness marker in syslog. health_checks(), which reports
a daemon that exited with a non-zero status, only runs after that wait.
A daemon that dies on startup therefore surfaces as "timeout waiting
for: ..." after 120 s (fabric manager) or 600 s (persistenced), and the
exit status that explains it is never reported. For example, fabric
manager exits with status 255 as soon as it rejects an item in its
configuration file.

Move the spawn-then-wait sequence onto NVRC as spawn_until_marker(),
next to spawn_daemon() and health_checks(), and replace
kmsg::wait_for_marker_after(). wait_for_marker() takes a check that
runs whenever no new line is available; spawn_until_marker() passes
health_checks(), so a non-zero exit now fails init at once, naming the
daemon and its exit status. A daemon that forks and exits 0 is still
accepted as before.

Signed-off-by: Jocelyn Berrendonner <jocelynb@microsoft.com>
Assisted-by: GitHub Copilot
---
 src/daemon.rs |  9 ++++-----
 src/kmsg.rs   | 51 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 src/nvrc.rs   | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 76 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/daemon.rs b/src/daemon.rs
index 25ad968..fb29a1c 100644
--- a/src/daemon.rs
+++ b/src/daemon.rs
@@ -3,7 +3,6 @@
 
